# GETPW(3) [deprecated]

## NAME

getpw - get name from UID

## SYNOPSIS

```c
int getpw(int uid, char *buf);
```

## DESCRIPTION

*Getpw* searches the password file for the (numerical) *uid*, and fills in *buf* with the
corresponding line; it returns non-zero if *uid* could not be found. The line is
null-terminated.

**Note:** it is declared at its own file head and by no header, which is this tree's rule for a
routine no v7 header names. Prefer getpwuid(3), which is what "deprecated" in the title has
always meant here.

## FILES

| /etc/passwd
| share/besm6/lib/libc.a, lib/libc/stdio/getpw.c

## SEE ALSO

getpwent(3), passwd(5)

## DIAGNOSTICS

Non-zero return on error.

## BUGS

*Buf* must be large enough for a whole line of /etc/passwd and there is no way to say how large
it is.

## BESM-6 NOTES

One v7 bug is fixed rather than carried. Two of the field walks were guarded against a `\n`
that cannot be present, the line having been read a character at a time and terminated already
\- so **a line with fewer than three colons walked off the end of the caller's buffer.** Both
walks stop at the terminator now.
